20: text += r'''
21: 
22: ## 7. Exact scalar-loop witnesses and the range
23: 
24: For (k=1), the new parameter is the original scalar itself:
25: (lambda=w). Take the literal oriented fan basis
26: [
27:  v=(1,0),qquad w_{
28: m fan}=(-4,1),qquad
29:  det(v,w_{
30: m fan})=1,qquad delta=(0,1)=4v+w_{
31: m fan}.
32: ]
33: Thus (S=13), and the actual positive scalar loop has
34: [
35:  [Sigma_{Phi,T}]=
36: rac{(13-1)(13-3)}4=30=2pmod {28}.
37: ]
38: This example uses the shorter family itself and does not select a cube root
39: of a homotopy-sphere class.
40: 
41: The exact (k=1) range is
42: [
43:                   {0,2,6,12,14,16,20,26}.                    	ag{OS.15}
44: ]
45: For an upper bound, the formula depends on odd (S) modulo 112. Evaluating
46: those 56 residues gives exactly the set displayed. Every value is attained
47: by the following primitive physical cocharacter pairs:
48: [
49: egin{array}{c|r|r}
50:  (a,b)&S=a^2-ab+b^2&[Sigma]pmod {28}\ hline
51:  (0,1)&1&0\
52:  (1,4)&13&2\
53:  (1,3)&7&6\
54:  (3,14)&163&12\
55:  (1,6)&31&14\
56:  (2,5)&19&16\
57:  (1,10)&91&20\
58:  (3,7)&37&26
59: end{array}
60: ]
61: These are actual fan coordinates. For any displayed coprime pair choose
62: integers (r_0,s_0) with (ar_0+bs_0=1), and set
63: (v=(b,r_0)), (w_{
64: m fan}=(-a,s_0)). Then
65: (det(v,w_{
66: m fan})=1) and (av+bw_{
67: m fan}=(0,1)=delta).
68: Thus each row supplies the required actual unimodular fan, with no
69: realizability inference from an unattained residue.
70: 
71: All values for every (k) are even: with (S=2j+1), (OS.3) is
72: (kj(j-1)). Conversely the fixed (S=13) fan gives (2k) modulo28.
73: As the actual cap order (m=3k) varies through the already constructed
74: positive integers, these shorter scalar families therefore realize exactly
75: the fourteen even classes. The proof of source-translation endpoint
76: minimality is retained separately with its explicit scope; it is not used
77: to infer these realized classes.
78: '''
